          }
        },
        "text_dkwwDP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-0",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-sm",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "95ch",
            "richtext": "<h6>How do air filters work?</h6><p>In a Blueair filter, ultra-thin polypropylene fibers of different sizes and layers are interwoven to lock in particles. Once captured, particles are never released back into your home or office environment, even when filters are heavily loaded. The filters capture larger particles like pollen, dust and pet dander as well as smaller particles such as microplastics and smoke. Because polypropylene prevents bacterial growth, our filters also prevent the growth of bacteria and mold inside the air purifier.</p><p><br/>When the filter needs to be replaced (around every six months), just open the lid, take out the old filter and put the new one in. No screws, hooks or tools are needed. All done in less than a minute. An extra bonus is that Blueair filters don’t require additives or washing. Polypropylene is also an environmentally responsible synthetic, which when properly disposed of, breaks down into carbon dioxide and water.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
